WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 line:0% align:end size:15%
<ruby><rt>kaa.lt</rt></ruby>

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:13.530
The Apothecary Diaries

2
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.410
This story is a work of fiction. The names of all of the characters, organizations, and so on
 are imaginary. It also bears no connection to any specific real-life events.

3
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.040
Apothecary! Come out right now!

4
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.720
Hey!

5
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:44.680
Open up!

6
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.250
What's going on? It's so early.

7
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.460
Episode 51: Let Them Eat Cake

8
00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.670
Hey! I know you're here!

9
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.840
Apothecary!

10
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.610
Someone's sick! Come to my house now!

11
00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.760
Hey!

12
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.980
Do you have money to pay?

13
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.130
What? Will you abandon us if I don't?!

14
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.860
You're an apothecary, aren't you?!

15
00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.570
Yes. And apothecaries charge for medicine.

16
00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.290
You'll take money from a poor person?!

17
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.860
Where's the old man who's always here?!

18
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.360
I guess dad showed some 
half-baked generosity.

19
00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.730
The old man is out making money.

20
00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.290
Go away if you can't pay.

21
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.170
We have to live in this run-down 
shack because of people like you.

22
00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.480
Always behaving like you 
deserve to get free stuff.

23
00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.400
Please. I'll pay you 
when I can, I promise.

24
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.790
My daughter is sick.

25
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.020
Chou-u, bring ink and a brush. 
And a wood plate.

26
00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.880
This is a bond. Can you write your name?

27
00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.340
I can't. What does it say?

28
00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.490
"I promise to pay for the medicine."

29
00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.550
Fine, just push your thumb on it. A stamp.

30
00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.020
Is this okay?

31
00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.870
Sheesh. Fine.

32
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.070
You seem kinda evil.

33
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.190
Ow! Ow...

34
00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.070
This way.

35
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.420
What are you doing out here?

36
00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.300
Sorry to make you come along, Ukyou.

37
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.120
It's a bother, but there's 
no way around it.

38
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.630
You're just like your dad after all.

39
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.600
We're here.

40
00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.800
Come in.

41
00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.350
I brought the apothecary!

42
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.050
Dad...

43
00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.510
This rotten smell...

44
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.090
How long has she been like this?

45
00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.880
A few days. But she's had issues 
with her hands for longer.

46
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.830
Please! Come on, take a look at her!

47
00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.210
What's that for?!

48
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.790
If I catch it too, 
this is all for nothing.

49
00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.000
I could walk away, you know.

50
00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.660
How protective.

51
00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.760
Now, about the symptoms...

52
00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.960
Looks like frostbite, 
but it's nowhere near cold enough.

53
00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.810
Dilated pupils. And...

54
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.140
She's worse than she was this morning.

55
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.320
Dad! What are we going to do?!

56
00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.200
She'll end up like Mom!

57
00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.160
No...

58
00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.370
Please! Save her!

59
00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.700
I can't afford to have less family!

60
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.450
Can't "afford" to, huh?

61
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.270
Did her mother die similarly?

62
00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.960
No, she died from a miscarriage.

63
00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.670
A miscarriage?

64
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.600
Did you feed her anything?

65
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.200
A bit of porridge.

66
00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.570
Almost no rice in here.

67
00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.120
What else did you add?

68
00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.840
Oh. To pad it a bit...

69
00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.460
Nothing wrong with those. Anything else?

70
00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.330
Well...

71
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.010
Nothing?

72
00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:24.160
Hey, what is that?!

73
00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.280
Where did you get that?!

74
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.800
Someone gave it to us.

75
00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.910
Mom said, "Let's eat it bit by bit, 
when there's nothing else to eat."

76
00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.600
She wanted to keep it a secret from Dad.

77
00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.930
I'm the head of this household!

78
00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:45.340
You don't even work, Dad! 
You just gamble and make us beg!

79
00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.640
You gamble away even the money we make!

80
00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.110
Tale as old as time.

81
00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.280
Show me.

82
00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.120
A sweet smell?

83
00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:09.050
Sugar. That's quite extravagant 
to give to a beggar.

84
00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.120
Who gave you this?

85
00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:15.450
I don't know. It was given to
 my sister, but she can't talk.

86
00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.980
When did you get it?

87
00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:21.460
It was before Mom died, 
so about a month ago.

88
00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:26.470
Who else got these snacks? 
Or who else had these symptoms?

89
00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.200
The old man living behind us.

90
00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.260
Got it.

91
00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:39.840
H-Hey! What are you doing to my daughter?!

92
00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.160
I'm taking her with me. There's no way 
she'd recover in a place like this.

93
00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.950
Also, get rid of that. 
It's the cause of the sickness.

94
00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:54.870
Maybe the miscarriage, too...

95
00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:01.270
I'll take her.

96
00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.160
The old man out back has 
fingers that have rotted off.

97
00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.390
I see.

98
00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:13.560
He tried to hide it, but started talking
 once I gave him some spare change.

99
00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.190
He said a woman gave it to him.

100
00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.470
Didn't see her face.

101
00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.040
Hmm. A woman.

102
00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.490
What's wrong with her? She's nasty.

103
00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.510
Then go boil some water.

104
00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.370
Here, for your trouble.

105
00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.180
It's not much, but...

106
00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:37.040
No need. I'm used to babysitting.

107
00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:40.640
See ya.

108
00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.740
I wish he stayed longer.

109
00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:50.800
Hey, why are her fingers weird-colored?

110
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.420
It's because of that baked snack.

111
00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.950
Or, more accurately, 
because of the ergot in it.

112
00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:57.680
We have some, too.

113
00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:58.560
Huh?

114
00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.400
It's used in abortion medicine, too.

115
00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:09.470
You can find it in bad grains, and it 
can cause issues even in small amounts.

116
00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.040
It restricts blood flow 
to the hands and feet.

117
00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.660
At worst, it causes them to rot off.

118
00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:16.710
It can also cause paralysis 
and hallucinations.

119
00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:18.330
Is it curable?

120
00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.820
Just stop eating ergot.

121
00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.420
And some exercise, I guess.

122
00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.700
That's it?

123
00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.020
That's it.

124
00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.820
In her case, what's more 
serious is malnutrition.

125
00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.500
Where's that hot water?

126
00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.340
Oh.

127
00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.360
Oh, and get some white rice 
from the old lady.

128
00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.430
White rice?! Got it!

129
00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.770
Oh, he forgot the hot water.

130
00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.300
The older sister probably 
didn't show symptoms

131
00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.380
because she held back and 
gave the snack to the little sister.

132
00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.190
The mother must have eaten it 
because she was with child.

133
00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:07.100
A snack containing sugar,

134
00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.670
and a mysterious woman 
giving it away to beggars...

135
00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.320
Something suspicious is going on.

136
00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:26.840
One, two.

137
00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:30.980
Wow! You're walking!

138
00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.950
Already acting like a big brother.

139
00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:41.380
Um...

140
00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:47.240
She didn't get those from a fall.

141
00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.040
My sister?

142
00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.290
Look.

143
00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:57.760
The money?

144
00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.470
Since your dad isn't here, 
I assume you didn't bring any.

145
00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.050
That's fine. 
I'll just sell off your sister.

146
00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:08.650
Huh?

147
00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:11.540
She's young enough to be taught.

148
00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.200
My sister can't talk. 
I'm worth more as a commodity!

149
00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:24.200
Oh, I assumed she'd try 
to appeal to emotion.

150
00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.700
Do you understand what you're saying?

151
00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.040
I know. At this rate, 
we'll be beggars forever.

152
00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.800
We'll probably be forced 
to be streetwalkers later.

153
00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:35.550
What little we'd make, 
Dad would take anyway.

154
00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:38.970
So, you'd rather just become 
a courtesan yourself?

155
00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.850
Yeah! You work at
 the Verdigris House, right?

156
00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.800
You want an introduction?

157
00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:45.850
Yeah.

158
00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:50.310
You really think you're worth that much?

159
00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.650
Same as my sister.

160
00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.240
She's younger. We can train her, 
and she'll learn quicker.

161
00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.860
She can't talk!

162
00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.530
Some gentlemen appreciate silence.

163
00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.890
But... I have to escape of this!

164
00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.330
I don't want to die stuck in the mud!

165
00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:07.710
No way...

166
00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.480
I'll never accept that!

167
00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.720
Another tale as old as time.

168
00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:21.660
But I do prefer the types 
who struggle and put up a fight,

169
00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.600
rather than sit around waiting 
for someone to rescue them.

170
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.520
What about your sister?

171
00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:28.280
I'll work for both of us.

172
00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.860
If I work hard enough, 
they'll take care of her too, right?

173
00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.860
If you're not useful, 
you'll both end up in the gutter.

174
00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:35.800
You okay?

175
00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.700
I know.

176
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.420
Is this...

177
00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.340
Use the well.

178
00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.260
Wash your hair too, even if it's cold.

179
00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.970
If you go with lice in your hair, you'll 
get smacked with a broom and tossed out.

180
00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:14.270
Who knows how she'll live 
her life from here on.

181
00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.690
But it's the path

182
00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.610
she chose to travel herself.

183
00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.290
If she ends up regretting it,

184
00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:35.140
she should just sink in the mud.

185
00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:42.920
Is something wrong?

186
00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.550
We got word from the Mi clan.

187
00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.680
From the spies?

188
00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.680
Yes. Look.

189
00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.150
Suspicious drugs are 
showing up on the streets?

190
00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.150
Shouldn't we crack down immediately?

191
00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:04.210
If we cause trouble without 
evidence, we will get overtaken.

192
00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.910
We need to catch them in the act.

193
00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.970
It doesn't seem like 
they've found the source yet,

194
00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.870
but they do note that 
a common thread exists.

195
00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.870
The "White Lady".

196
00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.620
White Lady

197
00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:18.630
The White Lady? I hear that name 
on the streets, occasionally.

198
00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:22.520
Dealing with the locust plague
 is urgent too, and yet...

199
00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.470
The books finally arrived.

200
00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.130
I must get them to Maomao right away.

201
00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.340
Master Jinshi, will you go in person?

202
00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.900
Yes. I wanted to get 
her opinion on this, too.

203
00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:38.020
About the court lady in the doctor role?

204
00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.030
But...

205
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.250
Master Jinshi is busy.

206
00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.040
Huh.

207
00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.280
That was random.

208
00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:00.550
Also, he still uses his eunuch name?

209
00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.050
I guess his real name 
isn't to be uttered lightly.

210
00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:08.250
Keeping the door open to show 
there's nothing suspicious going on

211
00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:11.600
is probably out of consideration 
as Master Jinshi's attendant, but...

212
00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.580
So much rabble.

213
00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.200
Here are the books from the stronghold.

214
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.970
Excuse me.

215
00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:29.780
Birds. Fish. Plants.

216
00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.530
I read the Plants book 
at the stronghold, but...

217
00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.200
Here it is.

218
00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.330
Insects: Vol. Two

219
00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.670
The Insects book.

220
00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.340
So, that contains information 
on locusts, right?

221
00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.640
It should.

222
00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:48.700
Does it not?

223
00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.860
No.

224
00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:53.810
Did anyone remove the books 
while they were in storage?

225
00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.140
Who would take interest in this?

226
00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.450
People like what they like.

227
00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:00.930
Did Sazen trick me?

228
00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.700
No, there's no benefit for him to do that.

229
00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:11.990
Oh, I'm sorry, there's some 
dust on your back.

230
00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.360
W-What was that?!

231
00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:18.750
It's still there. 
Please sit still, I'll get it.

232
00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:25.030
Seems like Pairin 
isn't getting enough action.

233
00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.760
She's too high-class 
to get customers every day.

234
00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:32.790
This would be fun to watch 
if Master Lihaku were here.

235
00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:34.030
Don't worry, just let me 
take care of everything.

236
00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:37.000
I'm leaving now!

237
00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.140
I already gave you what I needed to!

238
00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:43.400
Oh, no. I missed out on a first-timer.

239
00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.110
Bailed on his road to heaven.

240
00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.070
You mean hell.

241
00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.170
Anyway, what to do...

242
00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.700
Ukyou, have you seen Sazen?

243
00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.980
He's cleaning the front now.

244
00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.440
That's a servant girl's job.

245
00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:05.430
Yeah. If that's all he's willing to do,

246
00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.470
we can't keep him hired as a manservant...

247
00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.940
W-Why are you looking at me like that?

248
00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:21.640
Never mind that. You lied to me.

249
00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.340
There's nothing written here 
about locusts.

250
00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:26.410
No, that's not—

251
00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:28.280
Hey, where's the other book?

252
00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.280
Huh?

253
00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:32.520
There are supposed to be 
three books on insects.

254
00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:38.550
So, you're saying the stronghold 
never had a book on locusts?

255
00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:42.390
I'm sure it was there when 
the old apothecary was there...

256
00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.380
Maybe they put it in his coffin?

257
00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.610
That's a thing we do in my hometown.

258
00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:55.440
It's too bad that he died because 
of a failed experiment, though.

259
00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.600
Yeah. Experiments in immortality.

260
00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.730
There were experimental rats 
at the fortress too,

261
00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.780
but the medicine is supposed 
to be used on humans in the end.

262
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:07.590
You'd have to try it on humans 
to raise the chance of success...

263
00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:08.410
Hmm?

264
00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.860
Hey, what's wrong?

265
00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.550
Where did they process his remains?

266
00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:22.080
I-I don't know. She took care 
of those things.

267
00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:24.070
She?

268
00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:28.210
You know, that emotionless woman. 
The assistant.

269
00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:30.420
Ah!

270
00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.260
Ow!

271
00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:34.930
That's right, why didn't I think of that?!

272
00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.760
That woman must have seen it up close!

273
00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.910
I want to talk to her.

274
00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.250
If I ask Master Jinshi with a letter...

275
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.730
Hey! Give me back my daughters!

276
00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.470
You! You're...

277
00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:52.320
What kind of apothecary are you?! 
You sold them off!

278
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:56.020
Huh? I didn't sell them off. 
I had nothing to do with them.

279
00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:59.490
Besides, I didn't even 
get paid for the medicine.

280
00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:05.760
I even let you take a loan. 
I could ask for extra.

281
00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.310
Shut up!

282
00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:08.750
W-Wait!

283
00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.260
By "daughters," you mean those 
girls who are being tried out?

284
00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.020
Yeah.

285
00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.420
Dammit, move!

286
00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:15.810
Ow!

287
00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:17.260
You don't learn, do you?

288
00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.780
Ow!

289
00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:22.150
I hear a commotion, and it's you again.

290
00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:24.020
You're barking up the wrong tree!

291
00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:29.310
Shut up! They're my daughters! 
Mine!

292
00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:31.040
Cut it out.

293
00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.740
Oh, hey! It's Daddy!

294
00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.520
I've come to pick you up! 
Come on home, won't you?

295
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.880
Wha...

296
00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:58.300
W-Wait... Please!

297
00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.940
There's no way they can go home.

298
00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.180
They're the ones that came here, 
wanting to become courtesans.

299
00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:14.690
You're nobody to them.

300
00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:24.450
How am I supposed to live from now on?!

301
00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.670
Did you bring everything?

302
00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:36.670
Yeah.

303
00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.370
Hmm?

304
00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.600
See ya!

305
00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.990
You going somewhere? Take me with you!

306
00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.780
No. This is work.

307
00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.490
Not fair!

308
00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.690
Bleh!

309
00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:10.280
The surviving Shi clan children are there.

310
00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.200
I can't let him see them.

311
00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:19.210
Anyway, he was quick to agree 
to let me meet her so soon.

312
00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.470
Here we go!

313
00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:26.100
So simple.

314
00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:31.100
What would we do about Chou-u's future?

315
00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:35.960
If he weren't paralyzed, 
he could become a manservant here.

316
00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:39.860
Perhaps he can be an apothecary?

317
00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.990
Unfortunately, he doesn't 
seem interested at all...

318
00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.580
It's so much fun, though.

319
00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:08.400
The girl is coming to see you.

320
00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:11.490
I wonder what she wants with you, Rei.

321
00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:13.920
Yes.

322
00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:59.920
Next Time

323
00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:56.210
Next episode, "The Last Volume."

324
00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:59.920
Episode 52: The Last Volume

